\import{base-macros}

\p{\strong{Status:} open.}
\p{The changes in [log-Y5JW](log-Y5JW) were pushed to the branch of \pr{1} after other branches had been built on its first version. Nothing was rebased.}
\ul{
\li{The branch of \pr{13} adds a clause that no execution goes wrong to \code{\verb~|IR.Func.IsComputedBy~} and \code{\verb~|IR.Func.CorrectAt~} in \code{\verb~|LibcMath/Exhaustive/Reduction.lean~}. The review changed other parts of that file; a merge has to be made and built.}
\li{\code{\verb~|checkBlock~} of \pr{7}, in \code{\verb~|LibcMath/Exhaustive/Run/Block.lean~}, is the same computation as \code{\verb~|checkBits~} applied to \code{\verb~|checkRange.test O.check run mode~}. Keep one, and let the runner report \code{\verb~|checkRange.firstFailure~} when a block fails. See [ins-TZVS](ins-TZVS).}
\li{Resolved on 2026-11-23: \pr{1} was merged, so the journal and \code{\verb~|CLAUDE.md~} are on the main branch, and a branch gets them by merging it.}
\li{For the interpreter, see [prob-VFZQ](prob-VFZQ).}
}
\p{\strong{After the merge of \pr{13}} ([ses-UZN9](ses-UZN9)): \code{\verb~|Reduction.lean~} is merged and builds. Still to do: \code{\verb~|checkBlock~} in \code{\verb~|LibcMath/Exhaustive/Run/Block.lean~} and \code{\verb~|checkBits~} are the same computation, and the runner does not yet report \code{\verb~|checkRange.firstFailure~}.}
